,'54.36.148.148',395,'216.244.66.239',15),(640,658,'372',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TRANSFORMACIONI PROCESI PLIVAČKE TEHNIKE I PLIVAČKIH\r\nPERFORMANSI POD UTJECAJEM KONDENZOVANOG\r\nNASTAVNOG PROCESA','TRANSFORMACIONI PROCESI PLIVAČKE TEHNIKE I PLIVAČKIH\r\nPERFORMANSI POD UTJECAJEM KONDENZOVANOG\r\nNASTAVNOG PROCESA','The sample of this research consisted of 35 male, 20-24 years old, regular students\r\nof the second year of the Academy of Pedagogic Sciences (Department of sport)\r\nin Mostar. The significance of this paper is shows in the establishment of the condensed\r\nteaching process efficiency and its influence at the successfulness and the efficiency of\r\nbackstroke swimming technique. Results of the research showed that significant changes\r\nhappened in the swimming technique but there were no significant changes in the swimming efficiency.','N/A','Condensed program, efficiency, technique, swimming, students','N/A',NULL,'Solakovic, E. (2008). Transformacioni procesi plivaČke tehnike i plivaČkih\r\nperformansi pod utjecajem kondenzovanog\r\nnastavnog procesa. <i>Sport Mont, VI</i>(15-16-17), 496-500.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Avg_2008_Solakovic_496-500.pdf',9,'496-500',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'66.249.69.74',103,'5.43.68.177',7),(641,410,'231',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MOTORIČKE SPOSOBNOSTI UČENICA PRVOG,\r\nDRUGOG I TREĆEG RAZREDA OSNOVNE ŠKOLE','MOTORIČKE SPOSOBNOSTI UČENICA PRVOG,\r\nDRUGOG I TREĆEG RAZREDA OSNOVNE ŠKOLE','The aim of this research was to establish the motor abilities of female students\r\nfrom the fi rst, second and third grade of primary school. 254 female students from the\r\nprimary schools in Trstenik were tested for the research.\r\nMotor abilities were estimated according to seven variables (agility on the fl oor,\r\nforward bend on a bench, long jump from standing start, 30 m dash from a fl ying start,\r\n300 m run, the throwing of medicine ball, keeping in pull-up position).\r\nThe differences between female students of primary school were estimated\r\naccording to the multivariant analysis of variance.\r\nThe results of the research showed that, viewing from the aspect of motor abilities,\r\nthere are differences between female students from the fi rst, second and third grade of\r\nprimary school and they are statistically signifi cant.','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Zrnzevic, N. (2007). MotoriČke sposobnosti uČenica prvog,\r\ndrugog i treĆeg razreda osnovne Škole. <i>Sport Mont, V</i>(12-13-14), 121-128.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Maj_2007_Zrnzevic_121-128.pdf',8,'121-128',NULL,NULL,NULL,'123.125.71.102',84,'212.200.206.198',10),(642,511,'362',61,'362',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'EFFICIENCY OF STEP AEROBIC ON TRANSFORMATIONS OF\r\nANTROPOMETRIC CHARACTERISTICS MOTORIC ABILITIES OF STUDENTS','UTICAJ STEP AEROBIKA NA TRANSFORMACIJU\r\nANTROPOMETRIJSKIH KARAKTERISTIKA\r\nI MOTORIČKIH SPOSOBNOSTI STUDENATA','The main goal of this research is determining of effi ciency of two months step\r\naerobic training on quantitative differences in the area of antropometric characteristics\r\nand in the area of motoric abilities at students of Tuzla University. The size of sample\r\nconsists of 21 male student. It is visable from presented analisis, and results of two\r\nmonths-two times a week training, from the beginning and on the end of step aerobic\r\ntraining, tested with t-test, that there are evident effects in the area of antropometric\r\ncharacteristics and in the area of motoric abilities at students of Tuzla University','N/A','step aerobic, partial quantitative differences, univariant level, stenght,\r\nfi tness programm','N/A',NULL,'Djug, M., & Mikic, B. (2007). Efficiency of step aerobic on transformations of\r\nantropometric characteristics motoric abilities of students. <i>Sport Mont, V</i>(12-1