TAROSTI I TELESNE VISINE IGRAČA NA\r\nPRVENSTVU EVROPE ZA SENIORE U ŠVEDSKOJ 2003','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Jovanovic-Golubovic, D. (2004). Odnos izmeĐu igraČkih pozicija,\r\ngodina starosti i telesne visine igraČa na\r\nprvenstvu evrope za seniore u Švedskoj 2003. <i>Sport Mont, II</i>(2-3), 394-403.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Jovanovic_394-403.pdf',2,'394-403',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'220.181.108.147',132,'79.140.149.226',5),(1078,762,'562',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'JU JUTSU - SPORT BUDUĆNOSTI','JU JUTSU - SPORT BUDUĆNOSTI','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Kopas, J. (2004). Ju jutsu - sport buduĆnosti. <i>Sport Mont, II</i>(2-3), 412-420.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Kopas_412-420.pdf',2,'412-420',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'123.125.71.32',204,'137.74.207.188',4),(1079,885,'336',685,'336',519,'563',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'STANJE POSTURALNIH POREMEĆAJA I TELESNIH\r\nDEFORMITETA DECE MLAĐEG ŠKOLSKOG UZRASTA\r\nU OPŠTINAMA ZAJEČAR, KRUŠEVAC I ČAČAK','STANJE POSTURALNIH POREMEĆAJA I TELESNIH\r\nDEFORMITETA DECE MLAĐEG ŠKOLSKOG UZRASTA\r\nU OPŠTINAMA ZAJEČAR, KRUŠEVAC I ČAČAK','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Zivkovic, D., Milenkovic, S., & Drobnjak, D. (2004). Stanje posturalnih poremeĆaja i telesnih\r\ndeformiteta dece mlaĐeg Školskog uzrasta\r\nu opŠtinama zajeČar, kruŠevac i ČaČak. <i>Sport Mont, II</i>(2-3), 421-426.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Zivkovic_421-426.pdf',2,'421-426',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'46.229.168.131',478,'216.244.66.239',14),(1080,723,'537',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'AEROBNA SPOSOBNOST - OSNOVA\r\nPRIPREMLJENOSTI SPORTISTA ZA TAKMIČENJE','AEROBNA SPOSOBNOST - OSNOVA\r\nPRIPREMLJENOSTI SPORTISTA ZA TAKMIČENJE','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Radunovic, G. (2004). Aerobna sposobnost - osnova\r\npripremljenosti sportista za takmiČenje. <i>Sport Mont, II</i>(2-3), 427-429.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Radunovic_427-429.pdf',2,'427-429',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'46.229.168.144',367,'74.125.208.14',8),(1081,325,'406',512,'241',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'COACHES’ WORK EXPERIENCE AS AN INDICATOR OF MANAGEMENT\r\nATTITUDES IN KARATE','TRENERSKI STAŽ KAO ODREDNICA MENADŽERSKIH STAVOVA\r\nU KARATE SPORTU','Sports in general, which, self-understandably, implies karate as well, be longs to\r\nthat aspect of social improvement which focuses on satisfying individual and group needs,\r\nbut those of a country too. Karate does not yield any material value, but it creates certain values important for the whole society which can be materialsed by other processes. Just like any other field of work, recruiting particular management personnel in\r\nkarate is significant for indicating and positioning those needs that compel them to work\r\nin this very field. Therefore, one is certain: among the most significant factors that provoke\r\nactivity are motives and attitudes.\r\nIn today’s karate in Vojvodina particular managerial roles have not been well defined yet. The concept and strategy of a karate club as a basic organisational unit in sport is primarily based on knowledge, interests and motivation of a karate coach. Hence, there is a different motivational structure among those who are in karate.','N/A','coaches, karate, managers, attitudes','N/A',NULL,'Nesic, M., & Lolic, V. (2008). Coaches’ work experience as an indicator of management\r\nattitudes in karate. <i>Sport Mont, VI</i>(15-16-17), 897-904.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Avg_2008_Nesic_897-904.pdf',9,'897-904',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'220.181.108.155',348,'66.249.70.4',10),(1082,9,'137',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MOTORNO UČENJE – OD TEORIJE DO PRAKSE FIZIČKOG VEŽBANJA','MOTORNO UČENJE – OD TEORIJE DO PRAKSE FIZIČKOG VEŽBANJA','One of the “problems” that is currently present in physical culture in particular is\r\nthe issue of relationship between updating – innovations of technology of expert-pedagogical work in all its constitutive forms: physical education, sport, sports recreation etc.\r\nMotoric learning in educational process is the polygon of innovations both for the\r\nteachers – coaches and students, athletes and those who are involved in sports as recreation. The best evidence to this are the controversial attitudes as well as agreements of\r\nthe leading psychological theories that analyse the issue of learning within two groups: theory of linking and cognitive theory.\r\nThe present research focuses on such attitudes that, thanks to their updatedness,\r\ncontribute to understanding of the problem of transfer of knowledge and motoric skills\r\nin the way that does not result with their mutual exclusion but also through narrowing\r\nof their problem approach on to typical phases of motoric processing of information\r\nthat strengthen, namely weaken the established “open loop” (Sheffield), “closed loop”\r\n(Adams) and “pattern” (Schmidt) systems vie “attention”, “retention”, “motivation”\r\nand other elements of cognitive processing.\r\nOpening up of the issue on application of new but also tested ideas of motoric learning\r\nenriches the work on feed back information of subjects of educational process with a\r\nclear objective to strengthen the individual and incapacitate it to face its own capacities,\r\nknowledge and habits with »motoric problems« in order to start the journey towards the\r\nresolving of the same.','N/A','innovations, learning theories, motoric learning theories','N/A',NULL,'Milosevic, Z. (2008). Motorno uČenje – od teorije do prakse fiziČkog veŽbanja. <i>Sport Mont, VI</i>(15-16-17), 905-912.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Avg_2008_Milosevic_905-912.pdf',9,'905-912',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'66.249.69.74',436,'89.188.45.47',25),(1083,8,'333',22,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'TELESNA KOMPOZICIJA DECE SPORTISTA I NESPORTISTA','TELESNA KOMPOZICIJA DECE SPORTISTA I NESPORTISTA','Many children have inaccurate perception of their body weight and distort image\r\nof their body. This study has examined 30 girls as well as 60 boys at the age of 10-12.\r\nBody composition was assessed by Body Fat Analyzer “BES 200 Z” (Bioelectrical Sciences, Inc., CA, USA). According to he results, there are differences in morphological characteristics between non-athlete and athlete groups, while athlete groups of children are more likely similar.','N/A','body composition, physical activity, prepubertal age','N/A',NULL,'Obradovic, B., & Petkovic, J. (2008). Telesna kompozicija dece sportista i nesportista. <i>Sport Mont, VI</i>(15-16-17), 913-917.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Avg_2008_Obradovic_913-917.pdf',9,'913-917',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'66.249.69.74',422,'46.99.56.83',18),(1084,8,'333',4,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ANALIZA PARAMETARA DENZITETA KOSTI KOD DECE','ANALIZA PARAMETARA DENZITETA KOSTI KOD DECE','It is well known that physical activity has an anabolic effect to bone tissue. In order\r\nto determine the influence of different types of physical activity to the bone mineral density we have examined a group of boys and girls. All of the subjects were in prepubertal age at the early stage of achieving individual maximum bone mass. Bone mineral parameters of left and right calcane us were examined by Saharabone sonometer (Hologic\r\nInc., MA, USA). According to the results, we conclude that different types of physical\r\nactivity have different influence on bone mineral density at prepubertal age. Physical\r\nactivity at prepubertal age is very beneficial and should be supported.','N/A','bone mineral density, physical activity, prepubertal age','N/A',NULL,'Obradovic, B., & Bjelica, D. (2008). Analiza parametara denziteta kosti kod dece. <i>Sport Mont, VI</i>(15-16-17), 918-926.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Avg_2008_Obradovic_918-926.pdf',9,'918-926',NULL,'N/A',NULL,'220.181.108.171',573,'216.244.66.239',11),(1085,251,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'OLIMPIJSKI DUH KRUŽI CRNOM GOROM STO GODINA KANDIDATI','OLIMPIJSKI DUH KRUŽI CRNOM GOROM STO GODINA KANDIDATI','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Jovanovic, N. (2003). Olimpijski duh kruŽi crnom gorom sto godina kandidati. <i>Sport Mont, I</i>(1), 8-10.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Jovanovic_8-10.pdf',1,'8-10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'220.181.108.140',114,'147.91.1.41',11),(1086,252,'431',253,'431',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MODEL KOŠARKAŠKE UTAKMICE','MODEL KOŠARKAŠKE UTAKMICE','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Cvetkovic, L., & Kostic, V. (2003). Model koŠarkaŠke utakmice. <i>Sport Mont, I</i>(1), 11-19.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Cvetkovic_11-19.pdf',1,'11-19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'46.229.168.161',115,'147.91.1.41',8),(1087,254,'538',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'SOCIO-PSIHOLOŠKE OSNOVE GOJAZNOSTI KAO RIZIKO-FAKTORA','SOCIO-PSIHOLOŠKE OSNOVE GOJAZNOSTI KAO RIZIKO-FAKTORA','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Pajevic, D. (2003). Socio-psiholoŠke osnove gojaznosti kao riziko-faktora. <i>Sport Mont, I</i>(1), 20-27.','original scientific paper','SportMont_Dec_2003_Pajevic_20-27.pdf',1,'20-27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'46.229.168.152',108,'124.123.212.254',7),(1088,136,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'REFORME NASTAVNIH PLANOVA I PROGRAMA KADROVSKIH ŠKOLA ZA SPORTSKE TRENERE','REFORME NASTAVNIH PLANOVA I PROGRAMA KADROVSKIH ŠKOLA ZA SPORTSKE TRENERE','N/A','N/A','N/A','N/A',NULL,'Opavsky, P. (2003). Reforme nastavnih planova i programa kadrovskih Škola za sportske trenere. <i>Sport Mont, I</i>(1),